Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:30:45 +0300
Subject: mesa: S3TC DXT5 compression through libspeq on the PS3

Generic compressed RGBA requests (GL_COMPRESSED_RGBA: Teeworlds, TORCS, any game asking for
compressed alpha textures) and RGBA_DXT5 become DXT5, which Mesa encoded with its own encoder
on the PPE. libspeq (0011's hook, the same entry point with the DXT5 format) now encodes them
on the SPEs, or with its own PPE encoder for small images, with a colour block that never
relies on the 3-colour mode (DXT5's is always decoded in 4-colour mode). An older libspeq
returns -ENOTSUP for DXT5 and Mesa's encoder runs as before. The switch is libspeq's:
SPEQ_S3TC_DXT5=off gives DXT5 back to Mesa's encoder (SPEQ_S3TC=off all formats), no Mesa
rebuild.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c b/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
--- a/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
@@ -260,6 +260,10 @@ _mesa_texstore_rgba_dxt5(TEXSTORE_PARAMS)
 
    dst = dstSlices[0];
 
+#if DETECT_ARCH_PPC_64
+   if (!_mesa_s3tc_speq(GL_COMPRESSED_RGBA_S3TC_DXT5_EXT, 4, pixels, srcWidth, srcHeight,
+                        dst, dstRowStride))
+#endif
    tx_compress_dxt5(4, srcWidth, srcHeight, pixels, dst, dstRowStride);
 
    free((void *) tempImage);
